    de:limitation "OpenResearch does not record the execution environment (interpreter, OS, packages, hardware); local runs use the host's own environment and container images are mutable tags, so the record alone does not say how to reproduce the environment." ;
    de:limitation "Inputs outside the committed git snapshot and any random seeds are not recorded; only the command string and the committed code are." ;
    de:limitation "OpenResearch does not hash or register run outputs; the content digest in this record was computed by the adapter from a mutable local run directory at retrieval time." ;
    de:limitation "Run, experiment and project ids are random UUIDs local to one machine's store: there is no shared registry, and the run can be deleted by its owner (`orx exp delete`)." ;
    de:limitation "A run reaching status 'done' means the process exited 0. It says nothing about scientific validity and has not been reviewed." ;
    de:limitation "The database exit_code was NULL for this local run; the exit code was read from the run directory's exit_code file instead." ;
    de:limitation "This run read its inputs from, and wrote its outputs to, a directory OUTSIDE the OpenResearch snapshot and run directory. OpenResearch stores neither: the input and output digests here were computed by the adapter from immutable git blobs, and the run itself only links to them through hashes its own script printed." ;
    de:limitation "OpenResearch does not list a run's inputs. Replaying with one of two input files missing produced a different report without any error (measured during this import), so a replayer cannot learn the full input set from the record." ;
    de:limitation "The ensemble is mine (stated prior, three amplitudes, γ = 1, one family of initial perturbations, 1-D Neumann only). A different prior or perturbation family could give different rates; this is a sweep, not a claim about \"realistic\" parameters." ;
    de:limitation "Both solvers share equations. Solver disagreement (2.3%) is kept as unresolved mass, so the headline rates are bounded rates among all cells rather than among resolved ones." ;
    de:limitation "The analysis script was written after the sweep started (not after seeing results, with one exception: a smoke test of the analyzer on 14 partial rows printed provisional predictions; no design choice was changed afterwards). The PREREG text says \"about 08:40\"; the commit was made at 08:34 by `date`." ;
    de:limitation "The plain textbook formula (C0) is what predicts \"pattern whenever the continuum band exists\" regardless of domain; this sweep does not rank it against the gate, it asks about linear-theory limits only." ;
    de:limitation "No GPU or Nebius resources were used. The orx run logged only the analysis, locally." ;
    de:limitation "The orx run covers only the analysis step; the sweep itself ran outside OpenResearch under systemd-run and is not recorded there." ;
    de:limitation "Replay reproduces the analysis from the recorded report inputs; it does not re-run or independently check the 2,520-cell sweep (a separate GPU/CPU replay by the producer is planned, not done)." ;
